@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g8-fees-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-fees-draft`
IMPORT `g8-fees-as-made`
IMPORT `g8-fees-as-amended`
IMPORT `g8-fees`

-- g8-tests-dates.l4: the dates of the Fees Regulations, from the source.
--
-- Expected values, decided before any run from: the date of the gazette issue (9 July 2025 for Kovetz HaTakanot
-- 11951, 4 May 2026 for 12383), regulation 5 ("7 days from the day of their publication"), Interpretation Law
-- s 10(a) (the start day is not counted, so 9 July plus 7 is 16 July), Interpretation Ordinance s 17 (regulations of
-- legislative effect take effect on the day of publication where there is no other provision) and Interpretation Law
-- s 21 (the moment is 00:01 on the commencement day).  The wiki's note, "published 9.7.2025, commencing 16.7.2025",
-- and the note under s.63(a)(1) of the Law, "16.7.2025", agree.
--
-- The kinds of period met in this group, for the brief's ruling 4:
--   C  a commencement counted from another date: regulation 5 (7 days from publication).  IL s.10(c) is NOT applied
--      (the default for C); the alternatives are callable and tested below.  The amendment of 2026 is a commencement
--      with no period at all (Ordinance s 17 names the day of publication): IL s 10 has nothing to apply to.
--   R  a recurring calendar date: the update day, 1 January of each year (regulation 3(a)): outside IL s 10.
--   B  counted backwards: "the month before their commencement" (regulation 3(a)): outside IL s 10, so plain
--      calendar-month arithmetic on year and month numbers.
--   D, V, W: none is met.  Regulation 4 sets no time for paying; no figure has a period of validity of its own (the
--      interval in which a vintage is in force is delimited by two commencement dates, not counted); no window for an
--      application or a request is opened.
-- A Wednesday: 9 July 2025 and 16 July 2025 are both Wednesdays; 4 May 2026 is a Monday.

§ `Tests of the dates`

§§ `Regulation 5: commencement of the text as made (kind C)`

#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations as made were published on` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 9
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT NOT (`the Fees Regulations as made came into force on` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Fees Regulations as made came into force on` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 17)
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations made under section 59 came into force on` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16

-- 16.7.2025 is a Wednesday: `is weekday` is the daydate test (a check of the calendar facts above, not of the law).
#ASSERT `is weekday` (YMD 2025 7 9)
#ASSERT `is weekday` (YMD 2025 7 16)
#ASSERT `is weekday` (YMD 2026 5 4)

§§ `Alternatives for the fork on kind C`

-- Alternative 1: the commencement is the day after the seven days have run.
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on, taking the day after the seven days have run` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 17

-- Alternative 2: IL s.10(c) applied to the last day of the seven days.
GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`a calendar in which 16 July 2025 is a day of rest` MEANS
    `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2025 7 16)

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`a calendar in which 16 and 17 July 2025 are days of rest` MEANS
    `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2025 7 16), (YMD 2025 7 17)

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`a calendar in which only 15 and 17 July 2025 are days of rest` MEANS
    `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2025 7 15), (YMD 2025 7 17)

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`a calendar with no day of rest` MEANS
    `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on, applying IL s 10(c) under` (`a calendar in which 16 July 2025 is a day of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 17
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on, applying IL s 10(c) under` (`a calendar in which 16 and 17 July 2025 are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 18
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on, applying IL s 10(c) under` (`a calendar in which only 15 and 17 July 2025 are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on, applying IL s 10(c) under` (`a calendar with no day of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16

-- The taken reading ignores the calendar: with 16.7.2025 a day of rest, the taken date is still 16.7.2025.
#ASSERT NOT (`the Fees Regulations as made came into force on, applying IL s 10(c) under` (`a calendar in which 16 July 2025 is a day of rest`) EQUALS `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`)

§§ `Interpretation Law s 21: the moment`

#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations as made begin to bind at` EQUALS `the moment on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 59) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (`the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`) `binds`
#ASSERT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (`the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`) `binds`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2025 7 15) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (`the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`) `binds`

§§ `The 2026 amendment: commencement (AMc, kind C with no period)`

#ASSERT `the 2026 amendment of the Fees Regulations was published on` EQUALS YMD 2026 5 4
#ASSERT `the 2026 amendment of the Fees Regulations came into force on` EQUALS YMD 2026 5 4
#ASSERT NOT (`the 2026 amendment of the Fees Regulations came into force on` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 28)
#ASSERT `the 2026 amendment of the Fees Regulations begins to bind at` EQUALS `the moment on` (YMD 2026 5 4) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0

-- Another provision fixing a day would displace the day of publication; the amendment has none (NOTHING above).
-- With one (a day of 1 June 2026), Ordinance s 17 gives that day: the module's function, called as a check of the premise.
#ASSERT `Ordinance s 17 — the day regulations of legislative effect come into force, published on` (YMD 2026 5 4) `unless another provision fixes the day:` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1

§§ `Which vintage is in force`

-- Before 16.7.2025 none; the text as made from 16.7.2025 to 3.5.2026; the text as amended from 4.5.2026; never the draft.
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS JUST `the Fees Regulations as made`
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST `the Fees Regulations as made`
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2026 5 3) EQUALS JUST `the Fees Regulations as made`
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2026 5 4) EQUALS JUST `the Fees Regulations as amended`
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2030 1 1) EQUALS JUST `the Fees Regulations as amended`

-- At the moment level: the amendment binds from 00:01 on 4.5.2026, as made from 00:01 on 16.7.2025.
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force at the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 59) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force at the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0) EQUALS JUST `the Fees Regulations as made`
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force at the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 5 4) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 59) EQUALS JUST `the Fees Regulations as made`
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force at the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 5 4) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0) EQUALS JUST `the Fees Regulations as amended`

-- The day each vintage came into force.
#ASSERT `the day the Fees Regulations came into force, in` `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day the Fees Regulations came into force, in` `the Fees Regulations as made` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 7 16)
#ASSERT `the day the Fees Regulations came into force, in` `the Fees Regulations as amended` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 5 4)

§§ `Regulation 3(a): the update day (kind R) and the month before the commencement (kind B)`

#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the update day of the year` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the update day of the year` 2027 EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1

-- "The first update day after the commencement day": the next 1 January.  A commencement on 31 December has the
-- very next day as its first update day; a commencement ON 1 January has the next year's, the day itself not
-- being "after" it.
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the first update day after the commencement day` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the first update day after the commencement day` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the first update day after the commencement day` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the first update day after the commencement day` (YMD 2026 1 2) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1

-- The calendar month before the month of a day: July's is June; January's is the December before.
GIVETH A `Calendar month under regulation 3`
`June 2025` MEANS `Calendar month under regulation 3` WITH `year of the calendar month` IS 2025, `number of the calendar month` IS 6

GIVETH A `Calendar month under regulation 3`
`December 2025` MEANS `Calendar month under regulation 3` WITH `year of the calendar month` IS 2025, `number of the calendar month` IS 12

GIVETH A `Calendar month under regulation 3`
`February 2026` MEANS `Calendar month under regulation 3` WITH `year of the calendar month` IS 2026, `number of the calendar month` IS 2

#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the calendar month before the month of` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS `June 2025`
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the calendar month before the month of` (YMD 2025 7 1) EQUALS `June 2025`
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the calendar month before the month of` (YMD 2025 7 31) EQUALS `June 2025`
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the calendar month before the month of` (YMD 2026 1 5) EQUALS `December 2025`
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the calendar month before the month of` (YMD 2026 3 31) EQUALS `February 2026`
